From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergei Sveshnikov <sergei@svesh.dev>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 15:49:14 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 10/10] Service accounts: users for API tokens only

An agent or a script needs a token with a narrow set of rights, not a
person with an e-mail and a password.

- User field service_account (serde default false: old records are
  people). A service account has no e-mail, password or WebUI token;
  roles, account access and ACL work as for everyone.
- POST /api/v1/service-accounts (user:manage); listing, editing,
  removal and tokens go through the regular user and token APIs.
- Guards: login refused, password or e-mail cannot be set, only API
  tokens act for it (crates/core/src/users/service.rs).
- Web UI: "Service Account" button next to "Add User", the user form
  without e-mail and password, its token dialog opens after creation,
  a badge in the table, no MFA reset; en/ru.
- Tests: REST lifecycle, validation, guards, old records; schema test
  for the form. Checks: service account files in svesh-check.sh (own
  process: settings are set once per process), web job runs the users
  tests too.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
